## 🔴 Fix #2 — [MapComponent](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/MapComponent.tsx#34-127) prop mismatch

This fix has **two parts** — update the [MapComponent](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/MapComponent.tsx#34-127) to accept the new props, and keep the caller working.

**File:** [MapComponent.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/MapComponent.tsx)

**Find this code** (around lines 16–18):
```typescript
interface MapComponentProps {
  onDataLoaded?: (data: any[]) => void;
}
```

**Replace with:**
```typescript
interface MapComponentProps {
  centers?: { id: string; name: string; lat: number; lng: number; address: string }[];
  height?: string;
  onDataLoaded?: (data: any[]) => void;
}
```

**Then, find the function signature** (around line 34):
```typescript
export default function MapComponent({ onDataLoaded }: MapComponentProps) {
```

**Replace with:**
```typescript
export default function MapComponent({ centers, height, onDataLoaded }: MapComponentProps) {
```

**Then, find the `useEffect` that fetches from Firebase** (around lines 40–63):
```typescript
  // 1. Fetch and Normalize Data from Firebase
  useEffect(() => {
    async function fetchCenters() {
      try {
        // CRITICAL FIX: Match the collection name exactly with your Firebase Rules "recyclingCenters"
        const snapshot = await getDocs(collection(db, "recyclingCenters")); 
        
        const data = snapshot.docs.map(doc => {
          const raw = doc.data();
          return {
            id: doc.id,
            name: raw.name || "Unknown Center",
            address: raw.address || "No Address",
            lat: Number(raw.lat), 
            lng: Number(raw.lng)
          } as RecyclingCenter;
        });
        setRecyclingCenters(data);
      } catch (err) {
        // If this still fails, double-check your Firebase Rules "allow read"
        console.error("Firebase Permission or Fetch Error:", err);
      }
    }
    fetchCenters();
  }, []);
```

**Replace with:**
```typescript
  // 1. Use passed-in centers prop if available, otherwise fetch from Firebase
  useEffect(() => {
    if (centers && centers.length > 0) {
      setRecyclingCenters(centers as RecyclingCenter[]);
      return;
    }

    async function fetchCenters() {
      try {
        const snapshot = await getDocs(collection(db, "recyclingCenters")); 
        
        const data = snapshot.docs.map(doc => {
          const raw = doc.data();
          return {
            id: doc.id,
            name: raw.name || "Unknown Center",
            address: raw.address || "No Address",
            lat: Number(raw.lat), 
            lng: Number(raw.lng)
          } as RecyclingCenter;
        });
        setRecyclingCenters(data);
      } catch (err) {
        console.error("Firebase Permission or Fetch Error:", err);
      }
    }
    fetchCenters();
  }, [centers]);
```

**Finally, find the hardcoded height** (around line 121):
```typescript
      style={{ height: "300px", width: "100%" }} 
```

**Replace with:**
```typescript
      style={{ height: height || "300px", width: "100%" }} 
```

**Why:** Now the component accepts `centers` and `height` from the parent. If `centers` are passed (like from [PickupScheduler](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#138-444)), it uses those directly instead of hitting Firestore. If not, it falls back to the Firebase fetch.

