## 🔴 Fix #3 — Cancel race condition (UI gets stuck)

**File:** [PickupScheduler.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx)

**Find this code** (around lines 247–259):
```typescript
  const handleCancelPickup = async () => {
    if (!currentRequestId) return;
    setIsCancelling(true);
    try {
      await cancelPickupRequest(currentRequestId);
      setCurrentRequestId(null);
      setShowCancelConfirm(false);
    } catch (err) {
      setError('Failed to cancel request. Please try again.');
    } finally {
      setIsCancelling(false);
    }
  };
```

**Replace with:**
```typescript
  const handleCancelPickup = async () => {
    if (!currentRequestId) return;
    setIsCancelling(true);
    try {
      await cancelPickupRequest(currentRequestId);
      setPoolStatus('cancelled');        // ← Explicitly set status before clearing ID
      setCurrentRequestId(null);
      setShowCancelConfirm(false);
    } catch (err) {
      setError('Failed to cancel request. Please try again.');
    } finally {
      setIsCancelling(false);
    }
  };
```

**Why:** Previously, the code set `currentRequestId` to `null`, which kills the Firestore listener. If the listener didn't fire fast enough, `poolStatus` would never change to `'cancelled'` and the UI would stay stuck. Now we set it explicitly.

