## 🔴 Fix #6 — Drivers can't read user data (names/phones)

**File:** [firestore.rules](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/firestore.rules)

**Find this code** (around lines 7–8):
```
    match /users/{uid} {
      allow read: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
```

**Replace with:**
```
    match /users/{uid} {
      // Users can read their own profile
      allow read: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;

      // Drivers can read user profiles (to see customer name/phone)
      allow read: if request.auth != null && request.auth.token.role == 'driver';

      // Center staff can read user profiles (to verify customers)
      allow read: if request.auth != null && request.auth.token.role == 'recycling_center';
```

**Why:** The [DriverDashboard](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/pages/DriverDashboard.tsx#6-179) fetches customer names and phones via `getDoc(doc(db, "users", data.userId))`. Without this rule, every fetch would be denied and all customers would show as "Customer" / "N/A".

