## 🟡 Fix #7 — `isUploading` referenced before declaration

**File:** [Chatbot.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/Chatbot.tsx)

**Find this code** (around line 277):
```typescript
  const isUploading = uploadProgress !== null;
```

**Move it up.** Cut this line from line 277 and paste it right after the state declarations. Find this section (around lines 27–28):
```typescript
  const fileInputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
  const { user } = useAuth();
```

**Replace with:**
```typescript
  const fileInputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
  const { user } = useAuth();
  const isUploading = uploadProgress !== null;
```

**Then delete the original line 277** (now there'll be a duplicate — remove the old one that was further down in the file. It looks like `const isUploading = uploadProgress !== null;` sitting alone before the `return` statement).

**Why:** While technically this works at runtime due to JavaScript scoping rules, it's confusing and fragile. Moving the declaration near the top, next to other derived state, makes it clear and avoids any future issues.

